;;; A rule that could derive an activator binding a relation parameter to a
;;; fact loads and answers, since no run derives it — M1f **W59**, register
;;; row `W59/derived-activator-never` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`), filed by
;;; S1f.5.18 (T1f.5.18.1, 2026-11-09), `open` and owned by S1f.5.18, on the
;;; user's ruling of 2026-11-08 on Q-M1f.1 (*"Q1 - b"*), which chose the
;;; refusal knowing it refuses this program. It is S1f.5.5's probe
;;; `g14/derived-activator-never.ein`, `:why`s added.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `derived-activator.ein` without `(item (a b))`: `mk` derives `r`'s
;;; activator `(r ?f)` from `item`'s argument, a declared relation's, which can
;;; hold a fact, and `?f` is `r`'s parameter `?R`, which names a relation. No
;;; fact and no candidate puts a fact in `item`, so no run derives one.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The ruling (Q-M1f.1 (b)): some rule *could* derive an activator binding a
;;; relation parameter to a fact, which a static check sees at load, so the
;;; program is refused, as `derived-activator.ein` is: every command that
;;; loads it exits 1 with the loader's line (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers ────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The program loads and answers, exit 0: H is six candidates, `(box b)`,
;;; `(box z)`, `(hit b)`, `(hit z)`, `(item b)` and `(item z)`, and R is their
;;; cube, 64 states, the minimal line {∅} (`ein solve FILE` at `8249e872`,
;;; release and debug alike). A commitment to `(item b)` derives `(r b)`, a
;;; name, which binds `?R` as a relation parameter is bound.
;;;
;;; ── Since M1f S1f.5.18 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The loader refuses the program (T1f.5.18.3, 2026-11-09): every command
;;; that loads it exits 1 with one line naming `mk`, `r` and `?R` (`ein
;;; test`: 2), in either build, where it answered, 64 states. The register's `now` is that
;;; refusal; the section above is the record of the answer it replaced.

(relation box Node :why "{?1} is in the box")
(relation hit Node :why "{?1} is hit")
(relation item Node :why "{?1} is an item")
(box (a b))
(rule r (?R)
  :match (box (?R b))
  :assert (hit z)
  :why "a box holds a {?R} of b")
(rule mk ()
  :match (item ?f)
  :assert (r ?f)
  :why "{?f} is an item, so r is asked of it")
(query :goal (hit ?x))
